---
import SacredIcon from "../ui/SacredIcon.astro";
import SourcePanel from "./SourcePanel.astro";

const { topic, next } = Astro.props;

const coreFacts = [
  ["Misunderstood as", "Only death rituals", "document"],
  ["Deeper map", "Karma, rebirth, subtle body", "cycle"],
  ["Afterlife lens", "Journey of the jiva", "map"],
  ["Main insight", "Death as transition", "compass"],
] as const;

const domains = [
  ["Afterlife journey", "What happens immediately after death, the movement of the jiva, karmic transition, and higher paths.", "map"],
  ["Subtle body", "The traveler between lives is not the physical body, but a subtler continuity of impressions and tendencies.", "people"],
  ["Karma engine", "Action, intention, consequence, and rebirth are described as an ordered moral process across lifetimes.", "cycle"],
  ["Naraka realms", "Temporary hellish states or realms, interpreted literally, symbolically, or karmically across traditions.", "flame"],
  ["Reincarnation mechanics", "Desire, karma, and inner tendencies become forces shaping future embodiment.", "compass"],
  ["Preta lore", "Restless transitional states and the ritual importance of helping movement after death.", "bell"],
] as const;

const sequence = [
  "Death is not treated as simple disappearance.",
  "The jiva continues through a transitional state.",
  "Karma, desire, and impressions shape direction.",
  "The subtle body carries continuity between lives.",
  "Afterlife realms and Narakas become part of the karmic map.",
  "The larger goal remains liberation from compulsive return.",
] as const;
---

<article class="garuda-reading">
  <header class="garuda-hero">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Puranic atlas</p>
      <h1>Garuda Purana</h1>
      <p class="lead">Most people think the Garuda Purana is only about death rituals. That is only a small part of it.</p>
      <p>For Sanatana Path, the Garuda Purana is best understood as an afterlife atlas: a map of what continues when the physical body no longer does.</p>
    </div>
    <aside aria-label="Garuda Purana orientation">
      <span><SacredIcon name="map" size={30} /></span>
      <strong>Death is presented not as an ending, but as a transfer between states of existence.</strong>
      <small>Karma, desire, subtle embodiment, realms, and liberation become one connected system.</small>
    </aside>
  </header>

  <dl class="facts">
    {coreFacts.map(([label, value, icon]) => (
      <div>
        <SacredIcon name={icon} size={18} />
        <dt>{label}</dt>
        <dd>{value}</dd>
      </div>
    ))}
  </dl>

  <section class="opening">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">The hidden scope</p>
      <h2>Not just death rites. A map of transition.</h2>
    </div>
    <div>
      <p>The text opens a much wider field: cosmology, rebirth, karma mechanics, subtle body theory, realms after death, Narakas, time, Yugas, spiritual anatomy, and liberation.</p>
      <p>Many Hindu texts speak about Dharma, devotion, knowledge, time, and liberation. The Garuda Purana brings those questions into one of the most uncomfortable places: death.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="domain-grid" aria-label="Garuda Purana topic domains">
    {domains.map(([title, text, icon]) => (
      <article>
        <span><SacredIcon name={icon} size={20} /></span>
        <h2>{title}</h2>
        <p>{text}</p>
      </article>
    ))}
  </section>

  <section class="journey-map">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">How the idea moves</p>
      <h2>The journey is moral, subtle, and cosmic.</h2>
      <p>The unseen is not treated as vague emptiness. It is described as ordered, consequential, and connected to how one has lived.</p>
    </div>
    <ol>
      {sequence.map((item) => <li>{item}</li>)}
    </ol>
  </section>

  <div class="reading-body">
    <main>
      <section>
        <h2>Afterlife and post-death journey</h2>
        <p>The Garuda Purana gives detailed attention to what happens after death. It speaks about the journey of the jiva, the role of karma, the transition between births, the possibility of higher realms, and the consequences of one's actions.</p>
        <p>The person does not continue in the same visible form. Yet something continues: the jiva, shaped by karma, impressions, tendencies, and desire.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Subtle body technology</h2>
        <p>Hindu thought often distinguishes between the physical body, the subtle body, and the causal body. The physical body is visible and temporary.</p>
        <p>The subtle body is described as carrying impressions, tendencies, karma, and memory in seed form. This helps explain why rebirth is not simply about a body coming back. It is about continuity of subtle tendencies, unresolved impressions, and karmic momentum.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>The karma engine</h2>
        <p>The Garuda Purana contains one of the most detailed traditional discussions of action, consequence, rebirth patterns, and moral causation.</p>
        <p>Karma is not presented as random reward or punishment. It is closer to a universal accounting system operating across lifetimes. Actions leave consequences. Intentions matter. Habits become tendencies. Desires shape direction.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Naraka realms</h2>
        <p>The Garuda Purana describes numerous Narakas, often translated as hell realms or hellish states. This topic must be handled carefully.</p>
        <p>Traditional commentators and readers do not always interpret these descriptions in the same way. Some understand them as literal locations. Some understand them as temporary karmic states. Others read them symbolically as intense experiences produced by the consequences of action.</p>
        <p>The important difference from many eternal damnation ideas is that Narakas are generally understood as temporary.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Reincarnation mechanics</h2>
        <p>The text also explores how rebirth occurs. It connects rebirth with karma, desire, inner tendencies, and the conditions that influence future embodiment.</p>
        <p>One of the strongest ideas here is that desire itself becomes a force shaping future existence. What the mind clings to does not always disappear at death. Desire can become direction. Attachment can become momentum. Habit can become a path.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Cosmic geography of the afterlife</h2>
        <p>The Garuda Purana contains one of the most elaborate afterlife maps in Hindu literature. It describes paths after death, realms, messengers, cosmic judges, karmic transitions, and movement between worlds.</p>
        <p>Whether read literally, symbolically, ritually, or psychologically, the structure is striking. It gives death a geography.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Preta lore</h2>
        <p>One of the most misunderstood subjects in the Garuda Purana is the preta state. Pretas are often understood as restless beings or transitional states connected with unresolved movement after death.</p>
        <p>The mind-bending idea is this: not all beings immediately move to their next state after death. This is one reason ritual, remembrance, and correct transition matter in many Hindu traditions.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>What this teaches now</h2>
        <p>The Garuda Purana does not ask readers to obsess over death. It asks them to live with awareness.</p>
        <p>If action continues as consequence, if desire shapes movement, if the subtle body carries impressions, and if death is a transition rather than a wall, then life becomes more serious and more sacred.</p>
        <p>The point is not fear. The point is orientation.</p>
      </section>
    </main>
  </div>

  <SourcePanel sources={topic.data.sources} sourceNote={topic.data.sourceNote} traditionNote={topic.data.traditionNote} reviewedBy={topic.data.reviewedBy} lastReviewed={topic.data.lastReviewed} contentVersion={topic.data.contentVersion} />

  <a class="continue" href={`/atlas/${next?.slug ?? "cosmic-time"}`}>
    <span><small>Continue exploring</small><strong>{next?.title ?? "Cosmic Time"}</strong><em>Return to the connected atlas map.</em></span>
    <b>Explore next layer -></b>
  </a>
</article>

<style>
  .garuda-reading { position:relative; overflow:hidden; border:1px solid rgb(214 172 91/.18); border-radius:1.35rem; padding-bottom:1rem; color:#eee3cf; background:linear-gradient(180deg,rgb(2 9 15/.08) 0 28rem,rgb(2 9 15/.78) 46rem,rgb(2 9 15/.92) 100%),linear-gradient(90deg,rgb(2 9 15/.82),rgb(2 9 15/.32) 58%,rgb(2 9 15/.76)),url("/images/home/Garudapurana.png"),radial-gradient(circle at 82% 8%, rgb(173 124 255/.12), transparent 28rem),linear-gradient(145deg,rgb(8 19 28/.78),rgb(2 9 15/.62)); background-position:center top,center top,center top,center,center; background-size:auto,auto,cover,auto,auto; box-shadow:inset 0 1px rgb(255 255 255/.035),0 24px 80px rgb(0 0 0/.24); }
  .garuda-reading::before { position:absolute; inset:0; z-index:0; background-image:radial-gradient(circle, rgb(214 172 91/.11) 1px, transparent 1px); opacity:.52; background-size:34px 34px; mask-image:linear-gradient(to bottom, black, transparent 72%); content:""; pointer-events:none; }
  .garuda-reading > * { position:relative; z-index:1; }
  .facts,.opening,.domain-grid,.journey-map,.reading-body,.garuda-reading :global(.source-panel),.continue { width:min(100% - 2rem,72rem); margin-inline:auto; }
  .garuda-hero { width:min(100% - 2rem,96rem); margin-inline:auto; }
  .garuda-hero { position:relative; display:grid; grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1.25fr) minmax(18rem,.62fr); gap:0; overflow:hidden; border:1px solid rgb(214 172 91/.2); border-radius:1.2rem; padding:clamp(20rem,44svh,29rem) clamp(.9rem,2vw,1.3rem) clamp(.9rem,2vw,1.3rem); background:linear-gradient(145deg,rgb(2 9 15/.88),rgb(8 19 28/.7)); box-shadow:inset 0 1px rgb(255 255 255/.035),0 26px 80px rgb(0 0 0/.24); }
  .garuda-hero::before { position:absolute; inset:0 0 auto; height:clamp(20rem,44svh,29rem); background:linear-gradient(180deg,rgb(2 9 15/.03),rgb(2 9 15/.16)),url("/images/home/Garudapurana.png"); background-position:center; background-size:cover; content:""; }
  .garuda-hero::after { position:absolute; top:clamp(20rem,44svh,29rem); right:0; left:0; height:1px; background:linear-gradient(90deg,transparent,rgb(214 172 91/.28),transparent); content:""; pointer-events:none; }
  .garuda-hero > * { position:relative; z-index:1; }
  .garuda-hero > div { position:relative; min-height:clamp(18rem,32svh,25rem); border:1px solid rgb(214 172 91/.13); border-right:0; border-radius:1rem 0 0 1rem; padding:clamp(1.15rem,2.8vw,2.15rem); background:linear-gradient(135deg,rgb(2 9 15/.86),rgb(2 9 15/.5)),radial-gradient(circle at 82% 8%,rgb(214 172 91/.12),transparent 44%); box-shadow:inset 0 1px rgb(255 255 255/.035); }
  .garuda-hero > div::before { position:absolute; top:1.1rem; bottom:1.1rem; left:0; width:3px; border-radius:999px; background:linear-gradient(#f0b45f,transparent); content:""; }
  .eyebrow { color:#f0b45f; font-size:.68rem; font-weight:900; letter-spacing:.16em; text-transform:uppercase; }
  h1,h2 { font-family:var(--serif); font-weight:400; letter-spacing:-.03em; }
  h1 { max-width:12ch; margin:.3rem 0 1rem; font-size:clamp(3rem,5.6vw,5.7rem); line-height:.96; }
  .lead { max-width:52ch; color:#f2dfc0 !important; font-size:clamp(1.02rem,1.25vw,1.18rem); }
  .garuda-hero p:not(.eyebrow), .opening p, section p { color:#b6ada0; line-height:1.78; }
  .garuda-hero > div > p:not(.eyebrow):not(.lead) { max-width:62ch; color:#b9afa0; font-size:.98rem; }
  .garuda-hero aside { position:relative; min-height:clamp(18rem,32svh,25rem); border:1px solid rgb(214 172 91/.13); border-radius:0 1rem 1rem 0; padding:clamp(1.1rem,2.2vw,1.65rem); background:linear-gradient(145deg,rgb(6 16 24/.82),rgb(2 10 16/.56)),radial-gradient(circle at 18% 14%,rgb(214 172 91/.12),transparent 42%); box-shadow:inset 1px 0 rgb(214 172 91/.08), inset 0 1px rgb(255 255 255/.03); }
  .garuda-hero aside::after { position:absolute; right:1rem; bottom:1rem; color:rgb(214 172 91/.16); font-family:var(--serif); font-size:5.5rem; line-height:1; content:"?"; pointer-events:none; }
  .garuda-hero aside span { display:grid; width:3.25rem; height:3.25rem; place-items:center; border:1px solid rgb(214 172 91/.3); border-radius:50%; color:#f0b45f; background:rgb(214 172 91/.055); box-shadow:0 0 42px rgb(214 172 91/.13); }
  .garuda-hero aside strong { position:relative; z-index:1; display:block; margin:1rem 0 .65rem; color:#f7ebd3; font-family:var(--serif); font-size:clamp(1.25rem,2vw,1.75rem); font-weight:450; line-height:1.18; }
  .garuda-hero aside small { position:relative; z-index:1; color:#b9afa0; line-height:1.7; }
  .facts { display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr); overflow:hidden; border:1px solid rgb(214 172 91/.16); border-radius:1rem; background:rgb(255 255 255/.025); }
  .facts div { padding:1rem; border-left:1px solid rgb(214 172 91/.12); }
  .facts div:first-child { border-left:0; }
  .facts svg { color:#f0b45f; margin-bottom:.5rem; }
  dt { color:#99938a; font-size:.62rem; font-weight:850; letter-spacing:.1em; text-transform:uppercase; }
  dd { margin:.25rem 0 0; color:#e7d8bf; font-family:var(--serif); font-size:1.05rem; }
  .opening,.journey-map { display:grid; grid-template-columns:minmax(0,.75fr) minmax(0,1fr); gap:clamp(1.2rem,4vw,4rem); padding-block:2.7rem; border-bottom:1px solid rgb(214 172 91/.13); }
  .opening h2,.journey-map h2 { margin:.35rem 0 0; font-size:clamp(2rem,4vw,3.6rem); line-height:1; }
  .domain-grid { display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr); gap:.85rem; padding-block:2rem; }
  .domain-grid article { border:1px solid rgb(214 172 91/.14); border-radius:1rem; padding:1rem; background:linear-gradient(145deg,rgb(255 255 255/.035),rgb(255 255 255/.012)); }
  .domain-grid span { display:grid; width:2.5rem; height:2.5rem; place-items:center; border:1px solid rgb(214 172 91/.22); border-radius:50%; color:#f0b45f; }
  .domain-grid h2 { margin:.75rem 0 .45rem; font-size:1.28rem; }
  .domain-grid p { margin:0; font-size:.9rem; }
  .journey-map ol { margin:0; padding:0; list-style:none; counter-reset:path; }
  .journey-map li { position:relative; counter-increment:path; border-top:1px solid rgb(214 172 91/.12); padding:.78rem 0 .78rem 2.6rem; color:#d2c5b4; line-height:1.55; }
  .journey-map li::before { position:absolute; left:0; top:.78rem; color:#f0b45f; font-size:.7rem; font-weight:900; content:"0" counter(path); }
  .reading-body { padding-block:1.2rem 2rem; }
  main { width:min(100%,48rem); }
  main section { border-bottom:1px solid rgb(214 172 91/.12); padding-block:1.85rem; }
  main h2 { margin:0 0 .75rem; font-size:clamp(1.75rem,3vw,2.55rem); }
  main p { margin:.65rem 0 0; }
  .continue { display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:space-between; gap:1rem; margin-top:2rem; border:1px solid rgb(173 124 255/.24); border-radius:1rem; padding:1.1rem 1.25rem; background:linear-gradient(100deg,rgb(173 124 255/.08),transparent); color:#d7b8ff; }
  .continue span > * { display:block; }
  .continue small { color:#99938a; font-size:.62rem; letter-spacing:.1em; text-transform:uppercase; }
  .continue strong { font-family:var(--serif); font-size:1.55rem; font-weight:400; }
  .continue em { color:#aaa49a; font-size:.78rem; font-style:normal; }
  .continue b { font-size:.68rem; text-transform:uppercase; }
  @media(max-width:900px){ .garuda-hero,.opening,.journey-map{grid-template-columns:1fr}.facts{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}.facts div:nth-child(odd){border-left:0}.facts div:nth-child(n+3){border-top:1px solid rgb(214 172 91/.12)}.domain-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}.garuda-hero > div{border-right:1px solid rgb(214 172 91/.13);border-radius:1rem 1rem 0 0}.garuda-hero aside{border-radius:0 0 1rem 1rem}.continue{align-items:flex-start;flex-direction:column} }
</style>
